          %p
          %h2#section_Idea Idea
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theory"} type theory
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositions+as+types"} propositions as types
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositions"} propositions
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/types"} types
            are essentially the same: a proposition is identified with the type of all its
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proofs"} proofs
          %p
            However, this principle fails in many models of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin-L%C3%B6f+type+theory"} Martin-Löf type theory
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cubical+type+theory"} cubical type theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theories"} homotopy type theories
            based upon the two frameworks. Instead, they follow the weaker
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositions+as+some+types"} propositions as some types
            principle: while every proposition is interpreted as a type, not every type is interpreted as a proposition: only the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28-1%29-truncated"} (-1)-truncated
            types are interpreted as propositions (see
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/h-proposition"} h-proposition
            for more details).
          %p
            In this article, we create a dependent type theory where the full
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositions+as+types"} propositions as types
            principle holds: every type is an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/h-proposition"} h-proposition
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+types"} identity types
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositional+truncation"} propositionally truncated
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isProp"} isProp
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+type"} empty type
            corresponding to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/false"} false
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+type"} unit type
            corresponding to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/true"} true
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sum+types"} sum types
            corresponding to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjunction"} disjunction
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+types"} product types
            corresponding to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjunction"} conjunction
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+types"} function types
            corresponding to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/implication"} implication
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/negations"} negations
            to the dependent type theory, yielding a model of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intuitionistic+logic"} intuitionistic
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositional+logic"} propositional logic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/excluded+middle"} excluded middle
            or the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+negation+law"} double negation law
            yields a model of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+logic"} classical
            propositional logic.
          %p
          %h2#section_Presentation Presentation
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
            we shall be presenting here is similar to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objective+type+theory"} objective type theory
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Benno+van+den+Berg"} Benno van den Berg
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martijn+den+Besten"} Martijn den Besten
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/definitional+equality"} definitional equality
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/definitional+equality"} definitional equality
            means that the theory is both simpler, and behaves more like traditional
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositional+logic"} propositional logic
          %p
          %h3#section_Judgments_and_contexts Judgments and contexts
          %p
            The dependent type theory model of propositional logic consists of three judgments: proposition judgments
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} prop
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \; \mathrm{prop}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            to be a proposition, proof judgments, where we judge
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            to be a proof of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a:A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
            to be a context,
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ctx
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma \; \mathrm{ctx}
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a:A
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo :
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b:B
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c:C
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ctx
                  %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ctx
                      %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} prop
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi a
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ctx
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{}{() \; \mathrm{ctx}} \qquad \frac{\Gamma \; \mathrm{ctx} \quad \Gamma \vdash A \; \mathrm{prop}}{(\Gamma, a:A) \; \mathrm{ctx}}
          %p
          %h3#section_Structural_rules Structural rules
          %p
            The structural rules of this theory include the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/variable+rule"} variable rule
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weakening+rule"} weakening rule
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/substitution+rule"} substitution rule
          %p The variable rule states that we may derive a proof judgment if the proof judgment is in the context already:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi a
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Δ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ctx
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi a
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi a
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma, a:A, \Delta \; \mathrm{ctx}}{\Gamma, a:A, \Delta \vdash a:A}
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒥
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{J}
            be any arbitrary judgment. Then we have the following rules:
          %p The weakening rule:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi 𝒥
                      %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} prop
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi a
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi 𝒥
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma, \Delta \vdash \mathcal{J} \quad \Gamma \vdash A \; \mathrm{prop}}{\Gamma, a:A, \Delta \vdash \mathcal{J}}
          %p The substitution rule:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi a
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi 𝒥
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi 𝒥
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash a:A \quad \Gamma, b:A, \Delta \vdash \mathcal{J}}{\Gamma, \Delta[a/b] \vdash \mathcal{J}[a/b]}
          %p The weakening and substitution rules are admissible rules: they do not need to be explicitly included in the type theory as they could be proven by induction on the structure of all possible derivations.
          %p
          %h3#section_Dependent_propositions_and_dependent_proofs Dependent propositions and dependent proofs
          %p
            A dependent proposition is a proposition
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            in the context of the variable judgment
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:A
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊢
                    %mi B
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} prop
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:A \vdash B \; \mathrm{prop}
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B(x)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                  %mo :
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b:B
            in the context of the variable judgment
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:A
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊢
                    %mi b
                    %mo :
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:A \vdash b:B
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b(x)
          %p
          %h3#section_Equality_of_proofs Equality of proofs
          %p
            Equality of proofs of a proposition is represented by a proposition. This in other
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theories"} dependent type theories
            is called a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+type"} identity type
            or a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+type"} path type
          %p Formation rule for equality of proofs:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} prop
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi a
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi a
                      %msub
                        %mo =
                        %mi A
                      %mi b
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} prop
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash A \; \mathrm{prop}}{\Gamma, a:A, b:A \vdash a =_A b \; \mathrm{prop}}
          %p Introduction rule for equality of proofs:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} prop
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi a
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⊢
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} refl
                        %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mi a
                      %msub
                        %mo =
                        %mi A
                      %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash A \; \mathrm{prop}}{\Gamma, a:A \vdash \mathrm{refl}_A(a) : a =_A a}
          %p Elimination rule for equality of proofs:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi a
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi p
                      %mo :
                      %mi a
                      %msub
                        %mo =
                        %mi A
                      %mi b
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo ,
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} prop
                      %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi a
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi t
                      %mo :
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} refl
                        %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi a
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi p
                      %mo :
                      %mi a
                      %msub
                        %mo =
                        %mi A
                      %mi b
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi J
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi t
                      %mo ,
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo ,
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo ,
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma, a:A, b:A, p:a =_A b \vdash C(a, b, p) \; \mathrm{prop} \quad \Gamma, a:A \vdash t:C(a, a, \mathrm{refl}_A(a))}{\Gamma, a:A, b:A, p:a =_A b \vdash J(t, a, b, p):C(a, b, p)}
          %p Computation rules for equality of proofs:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi a
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi p
                      %mo :
                      %mi a
                      %msub
                        %mo =
                        %mi A
                      %mi b
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo ,
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} prop
                      %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi a
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi t
                      %mo :
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} refl
                        %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi a
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi p
                      %mo :
                      %mi a
                      %msub
                        %mo =
                        %mi A
                      %mi b
                      %mo ⊢
                      %msub
                        %mi β
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mo =
                            %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mi J
