          %p
          %h3#section_Existential_quantification Existential quantification
          %p
            Similarly,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/existential+quantification"} existential quantification
            is represented by a variant of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+sum+type"} dependent sum type
            where the dependent type hypothesis in the usual
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+sum+type"} dependent sum type
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
            is replaced by a predicate hypothesis. In the same way that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sum+types"} sum types
            are always propositionally truncated in propositional logic as a dependent type theory, existential quantification is similarly always propositionally truncated, due to the rules of propositional logic.
